  "body": "Stacked on #1684 (merge #1684 first)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added Option 1 (Slice 1) milling guard in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/wcs_page.rs`.\n- On `Kind::Mill` setups (`machine::kind_of(&state.world) == Kind::Mill`), `origin_fields` disables the `Tilt about X (roll)` and `Tilt about Y (pitch)` spinbuttons and shows a hint pointing to `Part alignment` on the Setup page.\n- `quarter_turns` renders the 3x2 turn buttons via `turn_row`, disabling `Turn X+`, `Turn X-`, `Turn Y+`, and `Turn Y-` on milling setups with the same hover hint.\n- `X origin`, `Y origin`, `Z origin`, `Turn about Z (yaw)`, `Turn Z+`, `Turn Z-`, `Level`, and `Set Origin` stay live on milling setups.\n- When an existing milling WCS is already tilted (`setup_wcs_tilt::setup_problem`), `wcs_page` warns that generation will refuse it and instructs the user to click `Level` and use `Part alignment`.\n- Non-mill machines (such as `Kind::Lathe`) keep X/Y tilt spinbuttons and all six quarter-turn buttons live.\n- Recorded the Option 1 choice and deferred items in `docs/decisions/1542-milling-wcs-tilt-guard.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nMilling generation refuses any WCS tilted off machine Z (`setup_wcs_tilt`), while the WCS page still invited users to tilt milling WCS axes via `Tilt about X (roll)`, `Tilt about Y (pitch)`, and X/Y quarter turns instead of using `Part alignment`.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pins in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/wcs_page_tests.rs`:\n  - `milling_setup_disables_xy_wcs_tilt_and_points_to_part_alignment`: red before fix (`Tilt about X (roll) must be disabled on a milling setup`), green after fix.\n  - `non_mill_setup_keeps_xy_wcs_tilt_and_turns_live`: verifies `Tilt about X/Y` spinbuttons and all 6 turn buttons stay live and `Turn X+` tilts the WCS on `Kind::Lathe`.\n  - Updated `quarter_turns_are_equal_buttons_filling_the_pane` so `Turn Z+`/`Turn Z-` are asserted live and `Turn X±`/`Turn Y±` disabled on `with_stock()` (`Kind::Mill`), keeping equal-size and alignment assertions intact.\n- Mutation checks on `crates/ui/src/egui_app/wcs_page.rs`:\n  - Reverted to `base-1684`: `milling_setup_disables_xy_wcs_tilt_and_points_to_part_alignment` (`Tilt about X (roll)`) and `quarter_turns_are_equal_buttons_filling_the_pane` (`Turn X+`) both failed; green after restore.\n  - Forced `turn_row` `enabled = true` and `tilted_mill = false`: both tests failed on `Turn X+`; green after restore.\n  - Forced `tilted_mill = false` alone: `milling_setup_disables_xy_wcs_tilt_and_points_to_part_alignment` failed missing the tilted-WCS warning; green after restore.\n- Gate and lint:\n  - `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (`14s`, `ui suites`: `ui lib`, `ui:boundary`, `ui:boundary_picks`, `ui:sinker_setup`, `ui:theme_files`, 0 failed).\n  - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: green.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Full cross-workspace gate beyond `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` (only `crates/ui` code changed).\n- Feature-pick Z-tilt guard (`wcs_pick_row.rs`) and MCP `set_wcs` milling guard (Slice 2, deferred because `#1931` is relocating `wcs_pick_row.rs`; `setup_wcs_tilt` continues to block tilted milling setups at generation).\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- Stacked on #1684 (`quarter_turns`, `turn_wcs`, and `wcs_page_tests.rs`); merge #1684 first, then retarget or refresh this PR.\n- Touches `crates/ui/src/egui_app/wcs_page.rs` alongside #1717 (`OFFSET_GROUP`, different functions/lines) and #1738 (`flip_row` inside `quarter_turns` between `Turn X-` and `Level`; this PR leaves widget placement between `Turn X-` and `Level` unchanged). Whichever merges later refreshes.\n\nChangelog: Disable X and Y WCS tilting on milling setups in the WCS pane and direct users to Part alignment on the Setup page.\n\nFixes #1542\n\n\n## Before and after screenshots\n\nBoth captures show the same milling setup with an existing 15° WCS roll, zero pitch/yaw, and 40×30×10 mm stock. These are actual egui page renders using a temporary CPU renderer because this host has no graphics adapter.\n\nBefore (`b94e2901`, parent of this change): X/Y tilt controls are enabled and the tilted-WCS warning is absent.\n\n![Before: milling WCS controls with an existing 15° tilt](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/48a03f38de7f937d4ff4409979e733115adbc432/2099/before-tilted-mill.png)\n\nAfter (`16450307`, current PR head): X/Y tilt controls are disabled. The warning explains that generation will refuse the tilted WCS and directs the user to Level and Part alignment on the Setup page.\n\n![After: disabled milling tilt controls and tilted-WCS warning](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/48a03f38de7f937d4ff4409979e733115adbc432/2099/after-tilted-mill.png)\n\nImages are stored only on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch at `48a03f38de7f937d4ff4409979e733115adbc432`. No screenshots or capture code were added to this PR branch.\n",
